Overview

Weld is robotics middleware written in Go. It speaks ROS 2 on the wire so Go programs join ROS 2 systems as first-class nodes.

The relation is CockroachDB to Postgres: same wire protocol and observable surface, different system behind it. Compatibility lives on the wire. Quality lives inside Weld.

Wire vs system

Unchanged on the wire:

- DDS RTPS with XCDR1 CDR
- Topic and type naming, type hashes
- Discovery and liveliness
- Standard messages, services, actions, parameters
- TF topics, /clock, bags on disk, launch arguments
- Every ros2cli verb

Replaced inside Weld:

- No rmw handles, no rcl wait sets
- No executor plus callback group split
- No Node versus LifecycleNode duality
- No global error state, no allocator plumbing
- No silent QoS mismatch

Operator view stays fixed. Implementation is free to differ.

Goals

- A Go native system an operator would choose even with no ROS present
- Bit level wire compatibility with CycloneDDS peers in v1, verified by interop gates
- Nav2 and MoveIt 2 run unmodified on Weld
- Every recurring ROS 2 failure class is structurally impossible, not merely handled

Non-goals for v1

- No source compatibility with rclcpp
- No intra process transport
- No zero copy loans or shared memory, except in-process loan honesty: the SDK and DDS loan paths detect loan-eligible types and refuse loudly elsewhere, with no shared-memory transport yet
- No bag storage engine, only exchange formats
- No FastDDS, Zenoh, or MQTT transports; the direct RTPS backend against CycloneDDS is the reference peer

One binary

Weld ships no C ABI. One Go binary talks to Humble, Jazzy, and Rolling by negotiating per peer: type hash presence, introspection topics, message hashes. Parsing is tolerant. Sending is strict. The version patchwork lives in transport backends. Core and the Go API stay single.

Build order

1. Foundations: types plus CDR plus hash plus fuzz
2. First contact: DDS unreliable round trip plus CLI echo
3. Matching: loud mismatch events
4. Visibility: graph index plus topic verbs
5. Calls: services with deadlines
6. Configuration: versioned store
7. Long tasks: action workflows
8. Second transport (post v1): Zenoh, then FastDDS and MQTT
9. Supervision, fidelity, soak

Each feature ships with three gates: unit tables with fake clocks, interop runs against rclcpp on CycloneDDS with ros2cli, chaos runs under race detection.
